WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.100
- So, let's bring out
our first guest, y'all.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.740
He is a four time Super Bowl champion

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.960
and five time Pro Bowler.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.130
Five times, geez.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.450
These days you can see him

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.000
as an analyst on Fox NFL Sunday.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.160
And he really let me down this season

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.390
because back in August,

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.730
this is what he promised me personally.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:21.090
- Team that you'd bet money
on to win the Super Bowl?

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.070
- Oh, I'm gonna go with
the Dallas Cowboys.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.020
They been making the playoffs every year.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.450
I feel like this is the year they just,

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.156
you know, get over that edge.

00:00:29.156 --> 00:00:31.980
(audience cheering)

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.343
- What we all thought.

00:00:34.343 --> 00:00:35.817
That's what I thought as well.

00:00:35.817 --> 00:00:39.450
Oh my God, I am in love with your suit.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.620
That's my favorite color.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.453
- Yes, yes.

00:00:41.453 --> 00:00:42.286
Green's your favorite color?

00:00:42.286 --> 00:00:43.119
- [Kelly] Yes, yes.

00:00:43.119 --> 00:00:43.952
- Oh, mine's red and blue.

00:00:43.952 --> 00:00:44.785
- [Kelly] It is?
- Yes.

00:00:44.785 --> 00:00:46.122
- Very American of you.

00:00:46.122 --> 00:00:46.955
- Yes, thank you.

00:00:46.955 --> 00:00:47.788
- Red and blue.
- Go USA.

00:00:47.788 --> 00:00:48.660
- Yeah.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:49.980
I used to love you

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.360
until you said the Cowboys were gonna win

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.040
and then look what happened.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:53.873
I don't understand.

00:00:53.873 --> 00:00:55.440
Everybody was saying that we were gonna,

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.410
look, we say it every year, I get it.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:00.990
But I really did think,
like we had all the players.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.550
It was all there.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.873
- I know, I did that
pick for you, too, Kelly.

00:01:04.873 --> 00:01:08.430
- Look, here's the thing,
I yelled so hardcore.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:10.830
I became that crazy fan, watch,

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.320
I got really into football this season.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.910
I'm like into fantasy football.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.140
Have you ever played fantasy as well?

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.145
- I've never played

00:01:17.145 --> 00:01:18.570
fantasy football ever.
- Really?

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.140
- I know all about fantasy football.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:20.973
- But you don't think about that.

00:01:20.973 --> 00:01:22.207
Like as a football player, you're like,

00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:24.840
"Man, what if these people
were all combined on one team?"

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.804
Well, you kind of had that because yeah.

00:01:26.804 --> 00:01:27.810
(audience laughing)

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.190
- I actually knew how it worked.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.680
And like throughout the
season when I was playing,

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:33.240
I always made sure I was like, okay,

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.770
if I can score a touchdown,

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.510
there's like two minutes
left in the fourth quarter,

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:38.520
we're already winning by
like three touchdowns.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.890
But if I can somehow
sneak another touchdown in

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:43.078
for my fantasy owners,
they're gonna love me.

00:01:43.078 --> 00:01:46.059
- That's what we say at
home, just walking in.

00:01:46.059 --> 00:01:47.640
And then when you start getting
angry at the other players

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.220
that you don't have, but it's so fun.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:52.200
Anyway, does it anger you that fans,

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.030
we use the word we?

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.595
We're like, "We lost" and
we didn't do anything.

00:01:56.595 --> 00:01:57.428
(audience laughing)

00:01:57.428 --> 00:01:58.261
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:58.261 --> 00:02:00.030
- Actually, no, it
doesn't anger me at all.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.230
Because without the fans,

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:03.905
we wouldn't have the NFL,
we wouldn't have the games.

00:02:03.905 --> 00:02:05.102
- Good answer.

00:02:05.102 --> 00:02:06.720
- So it's a collectivist.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.199
So, we make sense.

00:02:08.199 --> 00:02:09.032
- Okay.

00:02:09.032 --> 00:02:10.110
'Cause I feel insane at the end.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.030
My daughter's like, "Why
do you keep saying we?"

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:13.567
I'm like, "I used to be you, I know,

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:14.787
"but now I'm them."

